# Workspace-relative paths

Absolute filesystem paths under this repo (`C:\Users\…\locus\…`, `/Users/…/locus/…`) trigger Cursor Auto-review / safety blocks. Prefer paths **relative to the workspace root**.

## Prefer relative

Use workspace-relative paths for:

- Tool args: Read, Write, StrReplace, Delete, Grep `path`, Glob `target_directory`
- Shell `working_directory` / `cwd`, and paths passed to git, gh, pnpm, editors
- Docs, comments, commit messages, and Planka attachment or comment text that names repo files

```text
# ❌ absolute — often blocked
C:\Users\fifak\Documents\GitHub\locus\.cursor\rules\task-board.mdc

# ✅ relative to workspace root
.cursor/rules/task-board.mdc
apps/api
packages/shared
AGENTS.md
```

Forward slashes are fine on Windows in these tools.

## Exceptions (absolute only when required)

Use an absolute path only when the target is **outside** this workspace, for example:

- Global Cursor skills under `~/.cursor/skills-cursor` (or the OS equivalent)
- Temp files for `git commit -F` under `$env:TEMP` / `/tmp`
- Another git worktree when intentionally operating there — prefer `git -C <relative-or-worktree-path>` when a path relative to the current repo still works

Do not expand the workspace root into an absolute path "for clarity."

## Subagents

When prompting a Task / subagent, instruct it the same way: workspace-relative paths in tool args and written output; absolute only for out-of-repo exceptions above.
